The design for this work is in docs/nested-repos-design.md.

Done: GitIgnore (gitIgnore.d), GitRepos (gitRepos.d) and ParentDirectory
(parentDirectory.d) read, check, fix and write .gitignore and .gitrepos and
check the nested repos on disk; Finding (finding.d) and textFile.d support
them.

Next: the commands in docs/nested-commands-proposal.md (all its decisions are made), in steps:
1. nestedCommand.d (shared) - done.
2. check-nested - done.
3. remove-nested - done.
4. add-nested <directory>... - done; it replaces the old bin/add-nested, and add_nested.d and test_add_nested.py are deleted.
5. pull-nested.
6. add-nested --clone.
7. Clean-up: point bin/pull-nested at the new code, delete pull_nested.d (and debugio.d once nothing uses it), update the README, close #2 #3.

Replace the Python scripts with D, or delete them. Draft plan, to be decided per file:
